# Universal PC UI input vocabulary

**Authority:** [input-bindings.md § Universal PC UI vocabulary](../../docs/02-systems/input-bindings.md#universal-pc-ui-vocabulary), [ADR 009 amendment](../../decisions/009-input-bindings-pc.md#amendment-2026-06--universal-ui-vocabulary).

Hub, combat command UI, party menu, and tabbed pickers share one vocabulary. When a modal/overlay owns input, this table wins over exploration movement.

| Role | Keyboard | Mouse | Input System |
|------|----------|-------|--------------|
| Navigate / focus | `WASD` + arrows | Hover + LMB on control | `MenuNavigate` |
| Confirm | `Z` | LMB on control | `MenuConfirm` |
| Cancel / back | `X` | RMB | `MenuCancel` |
| Tab cycle | `Q` / `E` | LMB on tab chip | `*TabPrev` / `*TabNext` (scoped) |
| Menu / pause | `Tab` / `Esc` | — | `PartyMenu` / `Pause` |

**Mouse:** LMB on UITK `Button` = instant activate. `Z` = focus-then-confirm on same control. Combat LMB on command/target = instant queue (ADR 026).

## Exploration FPV exception

No overlay open: `WASD` = grid move, `Q`/`E` = turn — **not** tab cycle. `InputRouter` gates exploration turn/movement when party menu, pickers, or tab actions are active.

## Handler checklist

1. New menu surface → reuse `MenuNavigate` / `MenuConfirm` / `MenuCancel`; scope `Q`/`E` tab actions to overlay open only.
2. Wire **RMB** on `MenuCancel` (Hub + Combat maps) — do not fork a separate cancel path.
3. Hub **Tab** and **Esc** both toggle `PartyMenu` when safe.
4. Combat **Esc** → pause only when pause UI ships — never LIFO Back.
5. Global bind copy → `TabbedPickerRailHints` + `InputHints.Publish` — see `unity-global-input-hints.mdc`.

## Hint axis tokens (`TabbedPickerRailHints`)

| Navigator | Hint token |
|-----------|------------|
| 1D vertical rail/list | `[Up/Down]` (e.g. section rail, quit rows) |
| 2D or full `MenuNavigate` | `[Directional] Navigate` |
| Tabbed picker rows + tabs | `[Q/E] Tab` + `[Up/Down] Navigate` via `ForItemPickerRows` |
| Map autopilot cursor | `[Directional] Navigate` |

Prefer **Navigate** over **Command** / **Menu** / **Action** on hub and combat hints when `MenuNavigate` applies.

## Gamepad-ready layout (deferred)

**Authority:** [input-bindings.md § Gamepad-ready keyboard layout](../../docs/02-systems/input-bindings.md#gamepad-ready-keyboard-layout-deferred-implementation), [ADR 009 § Gamepad-ready amendment](../../decisions/009-input-bindings-pc.md#amendment-2026-06--gamepad-ready-keyboard-layout).

Keyboard defaults should mirror future gamepad groups:

| Slot | Keyboard | Gamepad (Xbox) |
|------|----------|----------------|
| Move / navigate | `WASD` + arrows | Left stick / D-pad |
| Confirm / interact | `Z` | A (south) |
| Cancel / back | `X` | B (east) |
| Secondary action | `C` | X (west) — expanded-map autopilot |
| Tertiary action | `V` | Y (north) — combat / battle log |
| Tab / turn | `Q` / `E` | L1 / R1 |
| Map toggle | `M` | View (Xbox); touchpad click (DualSense) |
| Menu / pause | `Tab` / `Esc` | Menu (Xbox); Options (PS) |

**System tier (outside face row):** `Tab` / `Esc` → **Menu** / **Options**; `M` (map) → Xbox **View** or DualSense **touchpad click** — not west face **`C`**, not **L3**. DualSense **Create** (`selectButton`) stays free when map uses touchpad.

Full table: [input-bindings.md § PC vs console reference](../../docs/02-systems/input-bindings.md#pc-vs-console-reference-locked-intent).

**Before adding a bind outside this table:** document it in the input-bindings audit table.
